    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1137">

                <pb facs="0817" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/62.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I hasten to thank you
                    for your letter of yesterday’s date in which you enclose copy of a telegram sent
                    by the State Department to its representative at El Paso, Texas, in regard to
                    the establishment of communication between Tampico and the American Fleet; and
                    to inform you in reply that I sent a telegram last night in the sense desired to
                    Sir L. Carden.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
